      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I wouldn\u0027t interpret that comment as written to mean that changes shouldn\u0027t go into AOSP, so clarifying would have helped me.\n\nUploaded https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/674516\n\n\u003e \n\u003e You could add an OWNERS file in AOSP that would ensure someone on the skia team gets a chance to review everything before it goes in.\n\nI\u0027m not sure that would work - we already have an `OWNERS` file in Skia, as well as an `OWNERS.android` file. `OWNERS` is a wildcard, which according to https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/443636 is necessary for enforcing code review.\n\nThe `OWNERS.android` file hasn\u0027t yet merged to AOSP, but it\u0027s also a wildcard, because we are unable to list our merge bot as an owner.\n\nIf we modified these files in AOSP, they might cause conflicts down the road.",
